C RS+cpp20
"Direction 2 (C11 forbids, C++20 allows) -- the C++20 model. Same shape as
 RS.litmus, but under C++20's weakened release sequences (P0982) the later
 same-thread relaxed store of 2 is NOT part of the release sequence headed by the
 release store, so an acquire that reads 2 receives no release: there is no
 happens-before to the data write. We model that absence of synchronisation by
 making the heading store non-releasing (relaxed) -- the relaxed store of 2 is
 exactly what the C++20 acquire sees, with no release attached -- so the stale read
 is observable.
   herd7 -model c11_orig.cat => Sometimes  (the C++20 outcome)
 Keeping the release AND counting it into the release sequence (the C++11 rule) is
 RS.litmus, which is Never. The two files bracket the P0982 change."
{ int data=0; int f=0; }
P0 (int* data, atomic_int* f) {
  *data = 1;
  atomic_store_explicit(f,1,memory_order_relaxed);
  atomic_store_explicit(f,2,memory_order_relaxed);
}
P1 (int* data, atomic_int* f) {
  int r0 = atomic_load_explicit(f,memory_order_acquire);
  int r1 = *data;
}
exists (1:r0=2 /\ 1:r1=0)
